# p-drag-over-handle (h11-p-drag): with h=2&k=4 the shift diamond sits at
# plane (2, 4), where P is: the marker beats the coincident handle (the
# hit test's last-index rule), so the hover there is the open hand with
# nothing lit (P has no onHover handler, so the diamond's hover never
# fires), and a drag there moves p and leaves h and k alone (no ruler out).
# The press is on the diamond's centre (1028, 290).
# Behaviour (read on ref-h11 at c6754e7, WebKit/Chromium/Firefox alike):
# the hover shot cursor grab-hover, the lit line empty, the url line
# h=2&k=4; the held shot cursor grab-active, the p line 3, the url line
# h=2&k=4&p=3; after the release cursor pan, the url line h=2&k=4&p=3.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
query h=2&k=4
wait 500
move 1029 291
wait 800
move 1028 290
wait 500
shot p-drag-over-handle-hover
down
wait 150
move 1078 290 over 160
wait 300
shot p-drag-over-handle-held
up
wait 600
shot p-drag-over-handle
